WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.831 --> 00:00:05.363
- When the doctors diagnosed
me, they told me that

00:00:05.363 --> 00:00:09.365
I wouldn't be able to clothe
myself or feed myself,

00:00:09.365 --> 00:00:10.755
that I would need
assistance for pretty much

00:00:10.755 --> 00:00:12.172
everything I did.

00:00:13.812 --> 00:00:16.387
My body is more than just a sack.

00:00:16.387 --> 00:00:20.079
It's actually an instrument
to do great things with,

00:00:20.079 --> 00:00:23.059
and I've been a professional
dancer for six years.

00:00:23.059 --> 00:00:26.559
(captivating flute music)

00:00:29.108 --> 00:00:33.981
I'm Jerron Herman, and I have
hemiplegia cerebral palsy.

00:00:33.981 --> 00:00:38.685
Cerebral palsy is a neuromuscular
disorder that affects

00:00:38.685 --> 00:00:41.746
messages going to the
muscles in your body.

00:00:41.746 --> 00:00:45.759
So the result is involuntary
motion and spasticity.

00:00:45.759 --> 00:00:48.510
Hemiplegia refers to me
because it affects only

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.593
the left side of my body.

00:00:56.457 --> 00:00:58.385
- [Instructor] Alright,
let me see you, please.

00:00:58.385 --> 00:01:01.002
- Heidi Latsky dance is
a company that integrates

00:01:01.002 --> 00:01:02.263
people with disabilities.

00:01:02.263 --> 00:01:04.383
- Ready, and one.

00:01:04.383 --> 00:01:06.142
(music plays)

00:01:06.142 --> 00:01:08.790
- I've always been an
advocate for those to pursue

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:13.251
the antithesis of the thing
that is their limitation.

00:01:13.251 --> 00:01:14.279
Why dance?

00:01:14.279 --> 00:01:17.185
Primarily because of the
physical diagnosis I was given.

00:01:17.185 --> 00:01:21.000
My body is the instrument,
and if I'm a disabled person

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.832
and my body's the instrument,
it's pretty audacious.

00:01:24.832 --> 00:01:27.999
(intense cello music)

00:01:31.376 --> 00:01:35.181
As I've been told, my arabesque is crazy,

00:01:35.181 --> 00:01:38.317
but it's from my left side,
and it comes from my left leg

00:01:38.317 --> 00:01:40.234
shooting up to the air.

00:01:41.885 --> 00:01:44.576
And my balance is based
on my right side being

00:01:44.576 --> 00:01:48.536
the main impetus for my
control, so that these things

00:01:48.536 --> 00:01:51.869
that were perceived as negatives are now

00:01:53.036 --> 00:01:55.453
folded into the choreography.

00:01:56.574 --> 00:01:59.991
When I am in the moment, and I'm dancing,

00:02:00.985 --> 00:02:03.985
I feel this calm that I've got this.

00:02:06.797 --> 00:02:10.852
Everything is working
together, and then some.

00:02:10.852 --> 00:02:15.019
Dance has relieved me of a
stereotype that is placed

00:02:16.027 --> 00:02:18.360
on people with disabilities.

